From: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: terminate and export the PCI device ID table

PCI ID matching walks until a zero entry. Without a sentinel, registering
the driver can read beyond the table and fault in do_pci_match_id on
unrelated PCI devices. Export the table for module alias generation too.

Signed-off-by: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
---
--- a/src/PCIE/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_pcie.c
+++ b/src/PCIE/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_pcie.c
@@ -23,7 +23,9 @@
 static const struct pci_device_id aic8820_pci_ids[] = {
     {PCI_DEVICE(AIC8800D80_PCI_VENDOR_ID,AIC8800D80_PCI_DEVICE_ID)},
     {PCI_DEVICE(AIC8800D80X2_PCI_VENDOR_ID,AIC8800D80X2_PCI_DEVICE_ID)},
+    { }
 };
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(pci, aic8820_pci_ids);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_WS
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3, 0, 0)
